PTC: complete the 303-order ledger, build the architecture, verdict FAIL

PART 2 - THE DATA GATE IS CLOSED

All 82 missing markets (83 orders) fetched. research/ptc_reconcile.py exits
zero on 13 hard assertions: 303 orders, 303 outcomes, 303/303 path coverage,
0 duplicate order/fill IDs, 0 unmatched fills, ledger +$9.3814, all 17
late-close markets carried, held-side agreement 1.0000 (naive 0.4765), close
derived from the ticker, every epoch in seconds and every order-to-close in
0-900s.

Missingness was outcome-correlated (+$153.78 matched vs -$144.40 unmatched)
and is now empty. Two structural causes: paths_full filtered on
result.isin(yes/no) against a truncated snapshot, dropping all 17 late-close
markets; and an 8<=ml<=14 entry gate dropped 65 more. That gate is correct for
defining eligibility but wrong for recovery - the PTC audit reads only `path`
and takes the held side from the ORDER - so it is relaxed and flagged.

Also fixed: fetch_missing_lsm_paths.py had no sys.path insert and could not
import capture.kalshi at all.

PART 3 - COMPLETE DOUBLE TEST, AND A CORRECTION v2 STILL NEEDED

v2 merged two clocks: probe_filled used the first COMPLETE one-minute candle
after the nominal wait, a mean 99.4s for a 60s design, so a probe filling at
75s scored as filled though the frozen rule cancels at 60s. v3 separates the
DECISION clock (wait + latency) from the OBSERVATION clock (first candle at or
after it, where the IOC is priced). Four orders reclassify.

  arm             submitted  fills  no-fill  commits  total    $/assigned
  CONTROL              4545    277       26        0  +$2.96      0.0098
  PROBE_ONLY_60         303    264       39        0  +$0.58      0.0019
  PTC_60                513    264       39       14  +$2.87      0.0095
  PTC_120               393    270       33        6  +$8.88      0.0293

CONTROL was +$140.41 on the 220-order cohort and is +$2.96 on the full
ledger, so the retracted "PTC minus control = -$119.70" was the survivorship
gap, not a property of PTC.

MECHANISM CONFIRMED, MONEY NOT. The no-fill branch wins 87.18% (60s) and
90.91% (120s) against 69.3% filled - the adverse selection really is
information, and it survives the complete ledger. But every comparison spans
zero across 5 fixed seeds: PTC_60-PROBE_ONLY P(<=0) 0.432-0.473,
PTC_120-PROBE_ONLY 0.234-0.252, PTC_60-CONTROL 0.505-0.613.

Concentration is disqualifying: dropping PTC_60's single best commitment turns
its IOC branch NEGATIVE (-$1.41). PTC_60 also fails leave-one-coin-out
(min -8.37) and leave-one-window-cluster-out (min -4.96).

PART 4 - INCOHERENCE FOUND AND DIAGNOSED

Adding 2s of cancel latency IMPROVES PTC_60 from +$2.87 to +$13.27. Isolated
to one order: KXETH15M-26AUG050415-15 fills at 61.69s, so a longer cancel race
catches it as a probe fill and deletes a commitment that lost -$11.16.

Slippage is non-monotone because cost is added BEFORE the 60-80c eligibility
test, silently deselecting trades. Holding the trade set fixed restores
monotonicity and shows PTC_60 goes negative at 2c: +2.87, +0.85, -0.52,
-2.22, -6.01.

PARTS 5-6 - ARCHITECTURE BUILT AND TESTED

capture/ptc.py: 16-state lifecycle manager, disabled by default
(PTC_ENABLED=0, PTC_LIVE_ENABLED=0), shadow/test mode needs no credentials.
139 tests pass, written before the implementation. Cancel timer starts from
exchange created_time; commit_allowed() fails closed without an affirmative
CANCEL_CONFIRMED at filled_qty==0; a fill inside the cancel race suppresses
the commitment; client_order_id is a pure function of (opportunity, phase) so
a crash between POST and persist adopts rather than resubmits; integer micros
only; every skip/block/error stays in the denominator. Fault injection covers
ten scenarios and none produces duplicate or excess exposure. Deterministic
replay of all 303 orders is byte-identical.

PARTS 7 & 9 - TRIAL SIZE AND RISK

  PTC_120 - PROBE_ONLY    2,272 windows/arm     ~95 days
  PTC_60  - PROBE_ONLY   98,088 windows/arm  ~4,087 days
  PTC_60  - CONTROL       2.1 billion         unreachable

PTC vs control is unmeasurable because the difference is ~zero against
CONTROL's $13.10/window dispersion. PTC's one clearly measurable effect is a
9x DISPERSION REDUCTION ($13.10 -> $1.49), not a higher mean.

Risk simulator: 100,000 chronological block-bootstrap paths per cell. Only q5
clears every stress scenario; q10/q15 fail adverse_blocks and q20 also fails
zero_edge. The first version allocated the full 100,000 x 2,160 matrix per
cell (~7 GB across 112 cells) and paged to disk; it now streams 5,000-path
chunks at ~740 MB peak for identical output.

PART 8 - VERDICT: FAIL

Gates 1, 8 pass; 10 passes at q5 only; 9 not run; gates 2,3,4,5,6,7 FAIL.
This is a mechanism PASS and a money FAIL and the two must not be conflated.
Only the prospective trial can settle it: PTC_120 vs probe-only, q5, ~95 days.

Account is $136.27 against a $211 floor; commit_quantity() returns 0 and the
machine reports KILL. Nothing here weakens that.

ptc_v2_report.md, PTC_STATUS.md and ptc_adversarial_v2.py are marked
SUPERSEDED with the reason and a pointer to research/results/PTC_FINAL.md.

